cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Conformalized time-series foundation models for commodity prices:
  an econometric audit across crisis regimes
message: >-
  If you use this software or the cached forecasts, please cite the paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahn
    given-names: Suho
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Business and Technology Management, KAIST
    email: dkstngh3502@kaist.ac.kr
repository-code: https://github.com/suhoahn-web/conformal-tsfm-commodities
abstract: >-
  Replication material for an audit of five time-series foundation models on ten
  daily commodity futures, 2015-2026, against a classical econometric panel under
  a Model Confidence Set, with predictive-interval coverage evaluated inside named
  crisis regimes and validated on a holdout window sealed before any model was run.
  Includes cached forecasts for every model-series-horizon combination, the
  evaluation and conformal code, information-set leakage tests, and the frozen
  pre-registration with its deviation log.
keywords:
  - commodity price forecasting
  - time-series foundation models
  - conformal prediction
  - model confidence set
  - forecast evaluation
  - crisis regimes
license: MIT
